  - language: 10
    solidName: Icosahedron
    solidFamily: Platonic Solid
    description: Twenty equilateral triangular faces meeting at each vertex. One
      of the five classical Platonic solids.
    fact1: Dual polyhedron of the dodecahedron.
    fact2: Used in D20 dice since ancient times.
    fact3: Geodesic domes approximate its shape at larger scales.
    natureEntries:
    - title: Viral capsids
      description: Many viruses, like herpes, form icosahedral protein shells.
      category: 1
    - title: Radiolaria
      description: Microscopic marine organisms build icosahedral silica skeletons.
      category: 1
    - title: Boron clusters
      description: The B12 unit in boron chemistry forms a perfect icosahedron.
      category: 0
